  "difficulty": 2,
  "prompt": "A physics simulation plots $y = \\tan\\theta$ for $\\theta$ from $0^\\circ$ to $180^\\circ$ and crashes at the one angle where the value is undefined. At what angle, in degrees, does it crash?",
  "answerType": "numeric",
  "primaryAnswer": "90",
  "alternativeAnswers": [],
  "acceptanceMode": "normalized",
  "hint": "Tangent is undefined wherever the cosine underneath it is zero.",
  "hints": [
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "Tangent is undefined wherever the cosine underneath it is zero."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "Between $0^\\circ$ and $180^\\circ$, where does cosine equal $0$?"
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "At $90^\\circ$, so the simulation crashes at $\\theta = 90^\\circ$."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "$\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ is undefined when $\\cos\\theta = 0$.",
    "On the interval from $0^\\circ$ to $180^\\circ$ the only such angle is $90^\\circ$.",
    "The graph has a vertical asymptote there, so the value the program tries to compute does not exist."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Watch the values run away",
      "steps": [
        "$\\tan 89^\\circ \\approx 57.3$ and $\\tan 89.9^\\circ \\approx 573$.",
        "The closer $\\theta$ creeps to $90^\\circ$, the larger the output, with no limit.",
        "At exactly $90^\\circ$ there is no number left to report — the function is undefined."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    "tangent",
    "asymptotes",
    "domain"
  ],
